THIRD-PARTY DATA AND MODEL ATTRIBUTION
================================================================================

The released model weights are derivative works of the following openly
licensed datasets. All are CC-BY-4.0, which permits commercial use with
attribution. Attribution is reproduced here as required.

1. NCT-CRC-HE-100K, NCT-CRC-HE-100K-NONORM and CRC-VAL-HE-7K
   Kather JN, Halama N, Marx A (2018).
   "100,000 histological images of human colorectal cancer and healthy tissue."
   Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1214456
   Licence: CC-BY-4.0

2. Collection of textures in colorectal cancer histology (Kather-2016)
   Kather JN, Weis C-A, Bianconi F, et al. (2016).
   Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.53169
   Licence: CC-BY-4.0

3. EBHI-SEG
   Shi L, Li C, Hu W, et al. (2022).
   "EBHI-Seg: A Novel Enteroscope Biopsy Histopathological Haematoxylin and
   Eosin Image Dataset for Image Segmentation Tasks."
   figshare. https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.21540159
   Licence: CC-BY-4.0
   (used only for the auxiliary segmentation model)

Pretrained backbone weights are obtained via `timm`
(https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models), Apache-2.0:
  - convnext_tiny.fb_in22k_ft_in1k        (Apache-2.0)
  - tf_efficientnetv2_s.in21k_ft_in1k     (Apache-2.0)
  - resnet34.a1_in1k                      (Apache-2.0)

